# Marrow asks where to keep your library the first time it starts, and it can be moved in Settings.
# Set DATA_DIR only to fix the folder instead (e.g. on a server); Settings then shows it read-only.
# Whisper and yt-dlp downloads stay in ./data/whisper (or DATA_DIR/whisper).
# DATA_DIR=/path/to/your/marrow-library
# Encrypts your AI keys in the database. 64 hex characters. Keep a backup: lose it and you must re-enter your keys.
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
APP_SECRET=
# Optional: public domain name(s) this server is reached by (comma-separated), and who may connect (default: this machine only)
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=marrow.example.com
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# Optional: port (default 5173)
# PORT=5173
